--[[
	The roster's new kinds (docs/kaiju-roster-expansion.md: 28 of its first
	thirty, and Skyjelly, number 57 on the second sheet, the starter
	support; the other 61, Prisma, Clawtide and kinds 31 to 90, are in
	Shared.KaijuRosterMore and merged in at the end). Each is a silhouette
	(Shared.KaijuModels), a role, a stat line, a fight style and three moves
	of its own. Shared.Kaiju, Shared.KaijuRoles and Shared.KaijuFight merge
	them in beside the first four kinds, so everything that reads those
	(battles, wild kaiju, cards, the HUD) knows them.

	A kind:
	  Name, Role, Blurb          as Kaiju.Species has them
	  Health, Damage, Rate, Speed, Reach, Guard   level 1, a Common Gemsoul
	  Habitat                    where it roams wild (Kaiju.wildKinds):
	                             Fringe (anywhere out past the core), Edge
	                             (the Edge only) or Vein (the guarded Rift
	                             Vein's guardian only)
	  Kit                        its own E, Q and R (Moves below)
	  Strike?                    a support's attack beside its kit (Key
	                             "Strike"; KaijuRoles.supportMoves)
	  Fight                      its fight style outside a battle
	                             (KaijuFight.Styles: blow names, timings,
	                             a heavy's share and arc, its guard)
	  Voice                      the first-four kind whose roar it borrows
	                             (CombatSound)

	Move IDs remain stable when a name or plan changes (saved Gemsouls use them).
	Moves: as KaijuRoles.Moves has them (Name, Key, From, IconSource,
	Description and Plan, Server.KaijuAbilities' shapes; an R's When).
	Origin names the model part a visual starts from; Projectiles makes a Storm
	fire from its body instead of the sky. Reach bounds each melee hit; Pose
	chooses the anatomical wind-up.
	Two flags those shapes take for these kinds: Heal (any shape: it heals
	this share of its own health as it casts) and Team (a Ward or a Mend:
	on every ally near it too, Radius studs).

	Pure data.
]]
